# What goes in the source distribution, beyond the code setuptools finds by
# itself.
#
# The default sdist picks up `tests/test_*.py` and nothing else, which is the
# worst of both worlds: half a suite that cannot run, because the fixtures it
# imports (`tests/property.py`, the `fake_mkvmerge.py` / `fake_ffprobe.py` /
# `fake_provider.py` stand-ins, `tests/selftests/`) were left behind. A
# distributor who runs the tests at build time - which is the reason to ship
# them at all - would see import errors rather than a verdict. So the sdist
# carries the whole suite, its fixtures, the docs the README links to, and the
# zipapp builder.
#
# The *wheel* stays code-only: `[tool.setuptools] packages/py-modules` decides
# that, and `organize test --unit` says so when the suite is not there.
graft tests
graft docs
include CHANGELOG.md CONTRIBUTING.md SECURITY.md LICENSE OVERHAUL.md REVIEW.md
include .env.example
graft benchmarks
include scripts/build_pyz.py
include __main__.py
global-exclude __pycache__ *.py[cod]
